experiment all-v2  —  16 trials  —  corpus v2
  Every runnable model on the honest split, against corpus generation v2 — the rebuilt corpus that recovered 924,315 ingredient occurrences the original normaliser missed. This is the complete leaderboard, and the thing it is meant to answer is whether better ingredient coverage changes the ranking or only the absolute numbers. The v1 leaderboard it is compared against is stored under runs/baselines/.
Declaration order is cheap first. A systemic problem — a stale split, a vocabulary mismatch, a metric returning chance for everyone — then shows up in the first thirty seconds rather than after item2vec has spent an hour earning the same failure.
All sixteen registered models run here. text-embed and text-aligned call a hosted embedding model and were previously unrunnable — llmmm-foundry deploys four chat models and no embedding model, and westus2 offers no OpenAI-format embedding at all. They are served instead by a text-embedding-3-small deployment on the ingredients-embed account in eastus, which is the only region in this subscription that carries it. Both need AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT and AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY in the environment.


